  "result": "The last gate run returned `WITNESS_FAIL`, and the cause is a mistake in the node's plan, not in the two files. Every witness passes except the planned `blind` one, and no scene can make that one pass.\n\n**What's written**\n- **Rule:** the subject is a vehicle. The rule applies when the subject is beside another vehicle b, not the subject, that is at rest within `p.edge_standing_gap` of a road edge lying on a highway, with b and the edge on the same side of the subject.\n  - The subject then may not be at rest unless one of these exceptions holds:\n    - traffic ahead in its lane within `p.queue_halt_gap`;\n    - a stop sign, yield sign, red traffic signal, active rail signal or gate, or a police officer signalling stop, governing a travel region the subject occupies.\n  - I added no narrowings of my own.\n- **Witnesses:** the 7 planned scenarios plus 7 added ones:\n  - `branch_4` to `branch_9`, one for each exception;\n  - `branch_10`, a mirrored left-side version of `forbid`.\n\n**Gate runs (2 of 6 used)**\n1. `CHECK_FAIL`: I had written \"same sign\" as bearing × offset > 0, and the unit check refuses comparing m² with m. I rewrote it as both-left or both-right and added `branch_10` to test the left-side case.\n2. `WITNESS_FAIL`: only `blind` fails. It expects unknown and gets violated.\n\n**Why the plan is wrong (span s9, scenario `blind`)**\n- The plan masks only `rel.bearing`. But Core works out the bearing itself from the two vehicles' positions and the subject's heading whenever the source doesn't supply it, so masking it changes nothing.\n- The rest of the applicability needs those same inputs: the edge's lateral offset needs the subject's position and heading, and b's distance to the edge needs b's position.\n- So whenever the rest of the scene is decided, the bearing is too. Removing a position or heading instead makes the result unknown for atoms the plan doesn't mask, and the gate rejects that.\n- **Fix for the plan agent:** mask an atom whose absence actually decides the verdict, such as `st.region_geometry`, which s11 already claims.\n\nI left `blind` as the plan describes it, so the failure stays visible when the harness re-runs the gate. I also made one stray call (the gate with `--help` added); it was blocked by the permission system and never ran.\n\nFiles are in `NRS_484B_450_1l`:\n- task_result.md",
